{
  "name": "Solar Stillpoint",
  "type": "feat",
  "img": "art/bbttcc/GOTTGAIT/BBTTCC%20Button%20Icons/BBTTCC_button_icon_fireball_1.png",
  "system": {
    "category": "technique",
    "source": "Bad Eden Originals (2025 rules)",
    "tags": [],
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>You become the place where violence goes to lie down.</em></p><p>Once per <strong>a Soma Break</strong>, as an <strong>action</strong>, you can invoke the Solar Stillpoint for <strong>1 minute</strong>:</p><ul><li><p>You emit a <strong>6 squares-radius aura</strong> of quiet golden light that moves with you.</p></li><li><p>Allies within the aura have <strong>advantage</strong> on defense check against being Shaken or charmed, and gain a <strong>+1 bonus to Guard</strong>.</p></li><li><p>When a creature within the aura would reduce another creature to 0 Integrity with a melee or ranged attack, you may use your <strong>reaction</strong> (no action cost for the attacker) to cause that blow to be <strong>non-lethal</strong>, leaving the target unconscious and stable instead.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Strategic Echo.</strong> If a major battle, uprising, or crisis under the Stillpoint ends with a no-fatalities victory, you may reduce an appropriate <strong>Darkness Track</strong> by 1, gain <strong>+1 Unity OP</strong>, and <strong>+1 Diplomacy OP</strong> as the story of “the day the war didn’t happen” spreads.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
